# Testing rules

## Mocking — at the network boundary only

- **MSW** intercepts at the network layer (covers axios via XHR adapter). Define handlers in `test/msw/handlers.ts` and the server in `test/msw/server.ts`.
- **NEVER** `jest.mock('@/lib/api')` or `jest.mock('@/queries/usePosts')`. Mocking our own modules hides regressions.
- Native modules (`expo-secure-store`, `react-native-mmkv`, `expo-notifications`) are mocked once in `test/setup.ts` — do NOT add per-test overrides without strong justification.

## Render with providers

Use a `renderWithProviders(ui)` helper that wraps in:
- `QueryClientProvider` with a fresh QueryClient (`new QueryClient({ defaultOptions: { queries: { retry: false } } })` — disable retries in tests)
- `SafeAreaProvider`
- `NavigationContainer` (with a stub stack)

Don't render bare components and pass mocked queries — that diverges from production.

## What to test

- One **user-flow test per screen** at minimum. "User taps submit → sees success message".
- Form schemas: import the Zod schema and assert `schema.safeParse(input)` for boundary cases.
- Custom hooks: render with `@testing-library/react-native`'s `renderHook` and assert state transitions.
- Navigation: assert that pressing a button calls `navigation.navigate(…)` with the right params.

## What NOT to test

- Implementation details (internal state, private methods).
- Component snapshots > 30 lines — they become noise.
- Library code (TanStack Query, Zustand) — trust the maintainers.

## Assertions

- Prefer accessible queries: `getByRole('button', { name: /submit/i })`, `getByLabelText('Email')`. They double as a11y audit.
- Avoid `getByTestId` unless no accessible alternative exists. If you use it, also add an `accessibilityLabel`.

## E2E with Maestro

- Flows live in `.maestro/flows/`.
- Tag smoke flows with `# tags: smoke` so CI can run a subset on PRs.
- Use `accessibilityLabel`-based selectors in the YAML — never raw text (breaks with i18n).
- Test data via env hooks: `MAESTRO_TEST_USER_EMAIL`, `MAESTRO_TEST_USER_PASSWORD`. Never check in real credentials.

## Coverage targets

- **Lines: 60%** floor across the repo.
- **Changed-lines: 70%** floor on PRs (CI gate).
- 100% coverage is not the goal — meaningful behavior coverage is.
